mw2coop patch for maps/_remotemissile.gsc (the Predator missile in Wolverines! and Contingency;
both levels carry the same script), Modern Warfare 2, 64-bit Steam build.

1. The UAV view after the missile sets the field of view with SetSavedDvar( "cg_fov", 26 ), which
   reaches both players' screens: the partner, running about with his rifle, zoomed in too. The
   pilot is noted in the dvar mw2coop_fov_pilot (maps\_mw2coop::fov_pilot), and the DLL keeps the
   other player's own field of view on his machine (src/fov.c). setClientDvar cannot do it: the
   engine refuses cg_fov there and drops the co-op session.
@@@ subst UAVRemoteLauncherSequence
SetSavedDvar( "cg_fov", 26 );
@@@ to
SetSavedDvar( "cg_fov", 26 ); maps\_mw2coop::fov_pilot( player );
@@@ end
@@@ subst ExitFromCamera_UAV
SetSavedDvar( "cg_fov", 65 );
@@@ to
SetSavedDvar( "cg_fov", 65 ); maps\_mw2coop::fov_pilot( undefined );
@@@ end

2. The drone view's caption ("CAMERA: DRONE_011") and the notices under it ("MISSILE LAUNCHED", "MISSILE RELOADED IN")
   are kept in the level variables level.text1 and level.text2: one slot for the whole level. With the laptop given to
   both players, the second player to open the drone view replaced the first one's reference, so when they left the
   view only the second player's caption was destroyed and the first player's stayed on his screen for good (an
   owner's screenshot of the Wolverines! roof: "CAMERA: DRONE_011" over the rifle). Each caption and notice is kept on
   the player it was made on (self.mw2coop_title, self.mw2coop_notice; every caller runs with the player as self).
@@@ subst text_TitleCreate
level.text1
@@@ to
self.mw2coop_title
@@@ end
@@@ subst text_TitleSetText
level.text1
@@@ to
self.mw2coop_title
@@@ end
@@@ subst text_TitleFadeout
level.text1
@@@ to
self.mw2coop_title
@@@ end
@@@ subst text_TitleDestroy
level.text1
@@@ to
self.mw2coop_title
@@@ end
@@@ subst text_LabelCreate
level.text2
@@@ to
self.mw2coop_notice
@@@ end
@@@ subst text_NoticeCreate
level.text2
@@@ to
self.mw2coop_notice
@@@ end
@@@ subst text_NoticeFadeout
level.text2
@@@ to
self.mw2coop_notice
@@@ end
@@@ subst text_NoticeDestroy
level.text2
@@@ to
self.mw2coop_notice
@@@ end

3. The weapon to go back to after the laptop is remembered whenever a player's weapon changes (it was noted only when the
   laptop is raised with the d-pad). A player whose laptop was raised any other way, or whose d-pad thread started late
   (player 2 got the thread late in Contingency), had no last_weapon: putting the laptop away ended in a script error
   (SwitchBackToMainWeapon compares the undefined value) and he stayed with the laptop in his hands.
@@@ subst remotemissile_weapon_change
self waittill( "weapon_change", weap );
@@@ to
self waittill( "weapon_change", weap );
		if ( !is_remote_missile_weapon( weap ) && weap != "none" )
			self.last_weapon = weap;
@@@ end
@@@ subst SwitchBackToMainWeapon_internal
if ( self.last_weapon == weapon )
@@@ to
if ( isdefined( self.last_weapon ) && self.last_weapon == weapon )
@@@ end
